# The gyroelongated pentagonal bicupola: the polynomial system of its optimum

`system`: 72 polynomial equations with rational coefficients in the 72 variables `x 0, …, x 71`,
with a closed rational interval for every variable. It has exactly one root in this box
(`Result.lean`). At the root

* `x 0` is the Nieuwland number of the polyhedron;
* `x 61, …, x 69` are the entries of the plug's rotation `R₁`, row by row;
* `x 52, …, x 60` are the entries of the hole's rotation `R₂`, row by row;
* `x 70, x 71` are the translation `t`

(`layout`); every interval of the box is beside its variable's name. A polynomial is a list of terms
`(c, [(i, e), …])` for `c * x i ^ e * ⋯`; an equation is a pair `(p, q)` for `p = q`
(`Definitions/Polynomials.lean`).
-/

